 lines=['# Single ReferDINO: HC and Vid finite joint parameter search','', 'Both target datasets use the existing exposed128-parent panels and seed41. One frozen ReferDINO supplies the same eight boxes for E_Ref initialization and OPD supervision. The original gamma1 initialization, Source, Strong, MBR, policy scales(0.05,0.25),32 candidates and8×256 temporary states are fixed. Network weights are not trained. The user allowed forward computation; the search reuses valid Source/expert inputs and actually replays the frozen decoder for every new optimizer path.','', '## Search and selection','', 'Coarse: lr0.003/0.01/0.03 × tau0.2/0.5;40-step paths read at10/20/30/40 and output alpha0.25/0.5/1/1.5/2. This is six optimizer paths and120 deterministic readouts per dataset. HC original40 baseline is reused after exact first-case replay; Vid40 baseline is actually run with all prior30 paths reproduced exactly. Each dataset then has one four-corner lr/tau sqrt2-neighborhood around its full-panel coarse winner, step±5 within1..40 and alpha±0.25. Coarse centers and original HC40/Vid30 configurations are retained.','', 'Output alpha scales the final center residual linearly and width/height residual in log ratio around E_Ref. It is a deterministic output parameter, not a new training rollout. Final recommended selection keeps the original severe-loss bound and prioritizes meaningful parent coverage among configurations within0.1pp of the best protected all128 complete mean; both mean winners are retained; no video-specific stop, alpha or method switch. GT is offline after each whole phase is sealed; it is never used in adaptation.','', '## Selected development configurations','', '| Dataset | lr | tau | steps | output alpha | initialization gamma | selected phase |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
